NAME
    shard - partition dotnet test units across parallel processes

SYNOPSIS
    shard [--shards N] [--keep-collections] [--head REV] [--tier T]
          [--repo DIR] [FILE]
    shard --machine [--head REV] [--repo DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.testing module. Reads an impact(1) selection
    from FILE or standard input, filters to dotnet units (excluding
    'lunap'), and distributes them across N shards (default: 4) using
    longest-processing-time-first bin packing so multiple 'dotnet test'
    processes can run concurrently.

    Measured durations come from the newest trial in the store (TRX or
    coverage run); unmeasured units default to 20 s, and unmeasured
    CLASS#KEY case groups default to 1/40 of their parent class time.

    Sources touching machine-wide shared state (virtual input/uinput,
    network listeners or fixed ports, fixed write paths, fixed lock
    files, or GPU queries) are detected statically and combined with the
    coverage map so all units touching machine-global state are pinned
    together in a single shard. By default, xunit collections
    ([Collection(...)], DisableParallelization) are split across
    processes since separate processes do not share in-process statics.

    Output is tab-separated:

        machine  N  NOTE                   Units pinned to the machine
                                           shard.
        shard    N  SECONDS  UNITS  FILTER Predicted duration, unit
                                           count, and dotnet filter.
        wall     SECONDS  SUM  NOTE        Longest shard, total time,
                                           and unmeasured unit count.

OPTIONS
    --shards N
        Target number of parallel shards (default: 4).
    --keep-collections
        Keep each xunit collection together as a single scheduling item
        rather than spreading it across shards.
    --machine
        List detected machine-global files and units with reasons,
        without reading a selection.
    --head REV
        Git revision used to scan sources (default: HEAD).
    --tier T
        Tier name; tiers other than 'nightly' append Category!=nightly
        to generated dotnet filters (default: land).
    --repo DIR
        Git repository root (overrides EMUSEN_REPO).

EXAMPLES
    impact --base main --head feature | shard --shards 4 --head feature
    shard --keep-collections selection.txt
    shard --machine | sort | uniq -c

EXIT STATUS
    0   Shard plan or machine-state report printed.
    2   Missing selection input, invalid options, or git/store error.

SEE ALSO
    impact(1), coverage(1), trial(1), units(1)
